{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"nan","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A NaN compares not equal, not greater than, and not less than every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value, including itself. Passing a NaN to an operation generally results"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in NaN."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let x = 1.21","\/\/ x > Double.nan == false","\/\/ x < Double.nan == false","\/\/ x == Double.nan == false"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because a NaN always compares not equal to itself, to test whether a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"floating-point value is NaN, use its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isNaN"},{"type":"text","text":" property instead of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"equal-to operator ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"type":"text","text":"). In the following example, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"y"},{"type":"text","text":" is NaN."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let y = x + Double.nan","print(y == Double.nan)","\/\/ Prints \"false\"","print(y.isNaN)","\/\/ Prints \"true\""]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/FloatingPoint\/nan"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/floatingpoint\/nan"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"A quiet NaN (“not a number”).","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/FloatingPoint"]]},"metadata":{"title":"nan","roleHeading":"Type Property","platforms":[{"name":"iOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"iPadOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"Mac Catalyst","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"13.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"macOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"10.10","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"tvOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"9.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"visionOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"1.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"watchOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"2.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false}],"required":true,"symbolKind":"property","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"nan","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"externalID":"s:SF3nanxvpZ"},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift":{"title":"Swift","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build apps using a powerful open language."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swift","kind":"symbol"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/FloatingPoint":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FloatingPoint","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A floating-point numeric type.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"FloatingPoint","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/floatingpoint","type":"topic","t